		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Temp. Cal and Batt Cal]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4758&amp;p=35132#p35132"><![CDATA[
Should Temp Cal and Batt Cal be part of calibration instead of General Options? My point is both of these values are not changing much. Once a user set the offset and it should be pretty much stay there. However, because both of them are part of General Options, when a user doing an options reset, or a new firmware came out with a requirement to do an options reset, these values are gone. And user might need to do some testing/measurement again to get the value back and put the offset back in the general options setting.<br><br>This is just my observation. I don't know if it is a good reasoning nor if it is possible to move them to another location, just an idea.<br><br>Charlie,<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Mon Jan 13, 2025 4:08 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
